==Trivia==
*Astro is designation M-002, with the '''M''' likely standing for {{Type|Main}}.
*Astro's [[Toon Handler]] is {{CI|Austin Russo|name=true}}.
*Astro's speech sound originates from [[w:C:Deltarune|Deltarune]] upon entering the [[w:C:Deltarune:Dark World|Dark Worlds]] in [[w:C:Deltarune:Chapter 2|Chapter 2]]. (This can be seen in [https://youtu.be/4ADeYLkC3Mc?t=378 this video], but in-game that sound is reproduced many times. Clear version of this sound can be seen in [https://youtu.be/mtVnm_OPHRU?t=1008 this video])
*Astro, {{CI|Dazzle|name=true}} and formerly {{CI|Squirm|name=true}} are a part of {{CI|Brightney|name=true}}'s Book Club.
*Based on a 1988 [[Astro/Gallery#Lore|photo]] found in the [[Greenhouse]] [[Floor]], Astro and {{CI|Dandy|name=true}} are heavily implied to be long-time friends. Their friendship is stated to be healthy, even after [[Gardenview]]'s downfall.
**This is also implied in a secret image found on the old official [[Merchandise]] website called [https://www.imsohappytheyrefriends.com/ imsohappytheyrefriends], where [[Dandy]] and Astro were looking at stars. This seems to be taking place in the Gardenview Lobby before it was painted and possibly before Gardenview opened.
***The image was updated on July 3, 2025, which altered the image with only one light on, [[Ichor]] leaking out of 2 off lights, [[Arthur]]'s and [[Delilah]]'s portraits are blacked out with what looks to be Ichor vines growing out of them, and there is text hidden in the dark reading "Wake up it wasn't like this". [https://web.archive.org/web/20241208045238/https://www.imsohappytheyrefriends.com/ Here] is the original version.
**They might still be friends as they still talk to each other, even during the Ichor operation, as implied in one of his interactions with {{CI|Pebble|name=true}} and {{CI|Teagan|name=true}}, as well as some of the other [[Toon]] interactions such as {{CI|Vee|name=true}} and {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}, but it isn't appreciated by all of them.
**According to his dialogue with {{CI|Connie|name=true}}, he and [[Dandy]] often chat about past episodes together, much to her lack of amusement. Astro appears nervous or worried about certain conversations that Connie may not have observed.
*It is theorized that Astro caught [[Dandy]] in his {{CI|Twisted Dandy}}[[Twisted Dandy|Twisted form]], due to Astro's obtainment requirements and Dandy's dialogue when buying Astro, in addition to his dialogue with [[Pebble]].
**When buying Astro from the shop, Dandy will say "{{Text|...}}", which may imply that Astro actually ''knows'' exactly what happened and what Dandy did, all because he caught him during the Ichor incident, but is afraid to talk to him about it out of that sinking feeling, even though Dandy himself is afraid of doing this because he thinks doing so would put their friendship at risk.
*He has many motifs themed around outer space, astronomy and magic.
**His name is a prefix used to describe stars, celestial bodies, and outer space in general.
**His face resembles the moon.
**The flash of a camera severely hinders healthy sleep, explaining his aversion to photography.
**Him having four arms (confirmed by [[Tisha]] and his official plushie), magical powers and outer space motifs vaguely but likely unintentionally implies he might be an alien.
**His connection with [[Dandy]] could be a reference to aliens and their interest in Earth.
**He can glow in the dark.
**He has telekinesis and [[w:c:powerlisting:Dream Manipulation|oneirokinesis]] (dream manipulation), two magic-related superpowers.
*Astro used to not be able to see the [[Toons]]' [[Stamina]] when they were under 50%, but the addition was made in [[Changelog|v0.4]].
**In [[Changelog|v0.13.14]], Astro's Active [[Ability]] cooldown was decreased from 75 seconds to 60 and his Passive Ability got the ability to see the exact percentage of Stamina a Stamina-deficient Toon has left.
*Astro used to have 2{{Star}} in [[Movement Speed]], before being bumped up to 3 Stars in [[Changelog|v0.2]].
**Similarly, his Active [[Ability]], {{AI|Astro|name=true}}, used to restore 50% Stamina of a user.
**In [[Changelog|v0.30.1]], he had a {{Star}}Star in [[Stamina]] moved over to [[Extraction Speed]].
***This makes Astro the only toon to have their stats changed in more than one update. 
*Astro is the first {{Type|Main}} that doesn't require [[Mastery]] on a [[Toon]] to be obtained and the only base-game Main to do so.
*Astro's full name was confirmed in the 10/18/2024 art stream.
*Astro enjoys sitting down and drinking hot chocolate (and iced tea, according to his [[Teagan]] interaction) from time to time.
*Before its release, Astro's {{Skin|Starry Night}} [[Skin]] had a slight model difference where his 'normal eye' was instead looking in the direction of his star eye instead of looking forward like the rest of his models do. The reason for this change is unknown.
*People playing as Astro used to experience chat bubbles being astronomically higher than their normal position, especially while using his Star-Time [[Skin]]. This is because Roblox included the actual size of Astro's hat (without the mesh) to be part of his height. This is more easily seen in Astro's T-Pose model, where the hat stands straight on Astro's head.
*Astro is the only [[Main Character]] and the first [[Toon]], along with {{CI|Scraps|name=true}}, whose requirement is to encounter a [[Twisted Dandy|specific Twisted]] who is not their [[Twisted Astro|Twisted counterpart]].
**This makes Astro the only Toon so far to require [[Research]] on two specific Twisteds.
**Additionally, he currently requires the lowest Research of a single requirement, being only 1% on [[Twisted Dandy]]. This means that it's not necessary to be seen by him in order to obtain Astro.
*The stars seen in Astro's extraction, Active [[Ability]], and 2nd idle animations are kept inside his body when walking around, though before his optimization in [[Changelog|v0.12.1]], they were stored in his head.
*Astro has the highest amount of Dialogues in-game, having 56. He is also the Toon that interacts most with other Toons, with the only exceptions being {{CI|Cocoa|name=true}}, {{CI|Flyte|name=true}}, and {{CI|Ginger|name=true}}.
*Astro is one of the [[Toons]] that has an official [[Merchandise]] plush as of now, with the others being {{CI|Boxten|name=true}}, [[Dandy]], {{CI|Poppy|name=true}}, [[Pebble]], [[Shelly]], [[Sprout]], [[Vee]], [[Gourdy]], {{CI|Bassie|name=true}}, [[Cocoa]], {{CI|Dyle|name=true}}, {{CI|Goob|name=true}}, [[Cosmo]], [[Gigi]], and {{CI|Eclipse|name=true}}.
**Additionally, the [[Skins]] {{Skin|Dino Snore}} Shelly, {{Skin|Lost Prince}} Gourdy, and {{Skin|Extra Cheese}} Pebble also have plushes.
*According to [[Qwel]], if Astro attempted to breakdance, he'd get hurt doing so, and make no further attempts to do so from that moment on. {{Small|(Needs citation)}}
*Astro's relationship with [[Boxten]] is implied heavily to be a fluctuating one in the [[Notes|lore notes]] and their interactions.
*Astro has more than one nightcap, shown in dialogue between him and {{CI|Gigi|name=true}}.
*In the new "Astro in Stage Fright" poster, the rest of the Book Club members are part of the audience. Only [[Dazzle]] appears there, as Razzle doesn't participate in the club's activities and instead sleeps for the duration of the club.
*In Astro's interaction with {{CI|Looey|name=true}}, Astro says that he sometimes gets stage fright. This is also shown in the "Astro in Stage Fright" [[poster]], where he (Looey) is only barely visible with one of his ears peaking out (though only because he's a background character, and not as an actual reference to Looey's shared phobia).
*Astro is the first [[Toon]] to wear a hat by default, and the first character to alongside his [[Twisted Astro|Twisted]] counterpart.
*After [[Changelog|v0.12.1]], Astro's design was slightly changed to include the black shorts seen in his [[Main]] [[Poster]].
**Weirdly, his in-game plushie didn't change, still missing his black shorts. However, his Care Bear plushie did have the shorts, so it is likely [[Qwel]] had forgotten to update the regular plushie.
*Astro and [[Shelly]] are the final [[Main Characters]] to be optimized post-release.
**[[Pebble]] got his optimizations in [[Changelog|v0.7.1]], [[Vee]] got her optimizations in v0.9.1, [[Sprout]] got his optimizations in v0.11.1, and finally Astro and Shelly got theirs in v0.12.1.
*Astro does not want to get changed out of his blanket due to how cozy he finds it, as seen in his interaction with {{CI|Brusha|name=true}}.
*Astro is the only [[Main Character]] that released in [[Changelog|v0.1]] to appear in the game icon.
*Astro, {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, and [[Shelly]] are one of the few [[Toons]] to have received [[Skins]] in the [[2025 Care Bears Collab]] and will never be unlockable again.
*Astro and [[Connie]] share some similarities:
**They are the only [[Toons]] to have 5 Star Stealth.
**Their light radius is the same.
***Due to all these similarities, some of Astro's code was used to make Connie. However, this brought over the 50% Stamina regeneration Astro gets from '''Well Rested''' into Connie's code as well. This was fixed later on.
**Their [[Twisted]] counterparts both seem to have sad expressions and cry (if not counting [[Twisted Connie]]'s attack face).
*In the [[Changelog|v0.12.1]] icon, Astro had a different texture in his face than the one used in his normal texture. This has also happened to [[Gigi]], [[Connie]], [[Razzle & Dazzle]], {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}, {{Skin|Grumpy Bear}} [[Shrimpo]], {{CI|Rodger|name=true}}, {{Skin|Wish Bear}} Gigi, {{CI|Finn|name=true}}, and {{CI|Waxwell|name=true}} in v0.4.1, v.0.5.1, v0.7.1, v0.10.1, v0.12.7, v0.13.14, v0.21.1, v0.22.1, and v0.25.1 respectively.
*Astro is the only [[Main Character]] to not have double letters in their full name, unlike [[Pebble|Pe'''bb'''le Dancifer Jr.]], [[Vee|V'''ee''' Version 1]], [[Shelly|She'''ll'''y Fo'''ss'''ilian]], [[Sprout|Sprout S'''ee'''dly]], [[Bobette|Bobe'''tt'''e Caroly'''nn'''e]], [[Bassie|Ba'''ss'''ie Bl'''oo'''mington]], and [[Gourdy|Gourdy Ho'''ll'''oway]].
*Astro is one of three [[Main Characters]] to be in the game on release, the other two being [[Pebble]] and [[Vee]].
*Astro appears to be friends with [[Vee]], [[Razzle & Dazzle]], and [[Brightney]] as implied by their dialogue.
*Astro acts as the guide for [[Dandy's World]]'s quest for [[The Hollow]] 2026, trying to get us out of the nightmare that is the quest.
*Astro was the only Book Club member to not get a [[Halloween]] [[Skin]] in [[Changelog|v0.29.10]], mostly due to him having a [[Skin]] already from the [[2025 Halloween Event]].
*Astro is the sixth [[Toon]] to get a [[Toon of the Week]], as well as the second [[Main Character]], and third male to do so.
**He is additionally the first Toon of the Week to have their [[Stats]] reworked.
*Astro is the second non-[[Holiday Toon]] to get an official song, the first being [[Connie]], but he is the first Non-Event [[Main Character]] to get one.
*Astro is the first [[Toon]] to have their [[Stats]] reworked twice.
*Astro is the second [[Toon]] to have his [[Ability]] go from an instant-use Active to a wind-up, the first being [[Ginger]].
*Astro is the first [[Toon]] to have many of his dialogues replaced.

